WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:21.839
Gerald and Kathleen were certain that the white towers belonged to an enchanted castle.

2
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.302
Jimmy was not so sure.

3
00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:33.068
They walked through a beautiful garden until they came to a maze.

4
00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:39.670
They tried to find the center of the maze.

5
00:00:43.573 --> 00:00:44.794
But it was impossible!

6
00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:46.656
"What's that?"

7
00:00:47.677 --> 00:00:50.019
Gerald picked up a red thread on the ground.

8
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.345
One end was tied to a thimble, but the other end "There is no other end!"

9
00:00:57.865 --> 00:00:58.786
Gerald realized.

10
00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.308
"Maybe it leads to something!"

11
00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:05.512
"I think the gardener put it there," said Jimmy.

12
00:01:06.804 --> 00:01:10.026
"Look at the crown on that thimble," said Kathleen.

13
00:01:10.046 --> 00:01:14.689
"Do you think a gardener would have a princess' silver thimble?"

14
00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:16.730
"Let's follow the thread."

15
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:21.253
Gerald walked forward, winding the thread around his fingers as he went.

16
00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:24.695
The thread led them into the middle of the maze.

17
00:01:26.135 --> 00:01:30.038
There they found a circle of green lawn with a sundial in the center.

18
00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:33.820
All around the edge of the circle was a marble seat.

19
00:01:36.372 --> 00:01:38.233
The thread ran across the lawn.

20
00:01:39.374 --> 00:01:42.316
It ended in the hand of someone sleeping on the seat!

21
00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:48.120
an enchanted princess!"

22
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.361
said Gerald.

23
00:01:49.381 --> 00:01:54.204
"Her clothes are so old-fashioned," said Kathleen.

24
00:01:54.224 --> 00:01:58.427
"She must have fallen asleep a hundred years ago."

25
00:01:58.447 --> 00:02:02.650
"She isn't really a princess," said Jimmy.

26
00:02:04.031 --> 00:02:05.512
Gerald and Kathleen laughed.

27
00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:09.850
They didn't care what Jimmy said.

28
00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:16.874
Every part of the adventure—the cave, the maze, the thread—felt magical to them.

29
00:02:16.894 --> 00:02:20.696
"Lift up the veil, Gerald," whispered Kathleen.

30
00:02:20.716 --> 00:02:25.299
"If she's beautiful, we'll know she's a princess."

31
00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:28.781
"Lift it yourself," he said.

32
00:02:29.961 --> 00:02:31.982
Kathleen gently lifted the veil.

33
00:02:32.002 --> 00:02:34.664
"Isn't she lovely?"

34
00:02:35.828 --> 00:02:37.949
"Not too bad," Gerald muttered.

35
00:02:37.969 --> 00:02:43.570
"Now, Gerald, you must wake the princess," said Kathleen.

36
00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:48.291
"She's not a princess," insisted Jimmy.

37
00:02:48.311 --> 00:02:52.193
"She's only a little girl dressed up like a princess.

38
00:02:52.613 --> 00:02:54.273
Look at how long her dress is.

39
00:02:54.693 --> 00:02:57.674
She won't be any taller than Gerald when she stands up."

40
00:02:58.674 --> 00:02:59.875
Kathleen ignored him.

41
00:02:59.895 --> 00:03:02.675
"Gerald, you're the oldest.

42
00:03:03.055 --> 00:03:04.376
You have to kiss her awake."

43
00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:06.580
"Not me!"

44
00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:07.841
cried Gerald.

45
00:03:07.861 --> 00:03:10.443
"She'll slap me the minute she wakes up."

46
00:03:10.463 --> 00:03:14.064
"Then I'll do it," said Kathleen.

47
00:03:14.084 --> 00:03:16.786
"But I don't think it'll do any good."

48
00:03:17.386 --> 00:03:18.207
And it didn't.

49
00:03:18.227 --> 00:03:22.889
"I don't mind kissing her," said Jimmy.

50
00:03:22.909 --> 00:03:25.831
"I'm not afraid like some people."

51
00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:31.114
With that, Jimmy planted a loud kiss on the princess' cheek.

52
00:03:32.094 --> 00:03:35.416
The three children stood waiting to see what would happen next.

53
00:03:36.476 --> 00:03:38.957
The princess opened her large, dark eyes.

54
00:03:39.938 --> 00:03:41.658
She stretched her arms and yawned.

55
00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:50.442
Then she said, "So the hundred years are over?

56
00:03:50.882 --> 00:03:52.683
Which one of you is my hero?"

57
00:03:52.703 --> 00:03:56.424
"I am," said Jimmy.

58
00:03:56.444 --> 00:03:58.425
"My prince."

59
00:03:59.046 --> 00:04:02.587
The princess held out her hand and Jimmy shook it hard.

60
00:04:02.607 --> 00:04:07.742
"But you aren't really a princess, are you?"

61
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:08.723
he asked.

62
00:04:08.743 --> 00:04:10.785
"Of course I am.

63
00:04:11.186 --> 00:04:12.267
Look at my crown."

64
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.930
She pulled aside her veil to reveal a crown of diamonds.

65
00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:20.675
"How did you ever get past the dragons?"

66
00:04:22.016 --> 00:04:23.497
Gerald ignored her question.

67
00:04:23.517 --> 00:04:26.780
"Then this really is an enchanted castle?"

68
00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.802
"Of course it is.

69
00:04:29.123 --> 00:04:30.184
Don't be stupid."

70
00:04:31.796 --> 00:04:35.377
The princess stood up and her dress fell in waves around her feet.

71
00:04:35.397 --> 00:04:39.398
"I told you her dress would be too long," said Jimmy.

72
00:04:39.418 --> 00:04:43.799
"It must have grown over the years," said the princess.

73
00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:48.681
"Let's go back to the castle, and I'll show you all my lovely jewels.

74
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:49.801
Would you like that?"

75
00:04:49.821 --> 00:04:52.482
"Yes," said Gerald.

76
00:04:52.502 --> 00:04:55.543
"But "But what?"

77
00:04:56.063 --> 00:04:57.743
The princess sounded impatient.

78
00:04:59.224 --> 00:05:00.424
"But we're awfully hungry.

79
00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.361
We never got to eat our lunch."

80
00:05:03.461 --> 00:05:05.302
The princess looked at the sundial.

81
00:05:05.942 --> 00:05:06.923
It was three o'clock.

82
00:05:08.023 --> 00:05:09.864
"You've had nothing to eat for hours.

83
00:05:10.224 --> 00:05:11.044
But think of me.

84
00:05:11.505 --> 00:05:13.786
I've had nothing to eat for a hundred years!"
